    "https://sunyopt.peopleadmin.com/postings/2594": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant Department of Biological and Vision Sciences",
      "description": "SUNY College of Optometry | Administrative Assistant Department of Biological and Vision Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Assistant Department of Biological and Vision Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant Department of Biological and Vision Sciences Position Description SUNY College of Optometry seeks a highly organized, proactive, and experienced Administrative Assistant to support the Chairperson and Department of Biological and Vision Sciences ( BVS ). The Department of BVS delivers the foundational basic science curriculum that supports the Doctor of Optometry program. Reporting directly to the Department Chair, the Administrative Assistant serves as the department’s primary administrative professional and plays a critical role in ensuring efficient day-to-day operations. The successful candidate will have strong administrative and organizational skills, exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and manage multiple priorities effectively in a dynamic academic environment. This position oversees departmental office operations, coordinates communications, supports budgetary and fiscal activities, supervises office support staff and work-study students, maintains departmental records, and provides comprehensive administrative support to faculty, students, and departmental leadership. The Administrative Assistant will work collaboratively with faculty and staff across the College to support the department’s academic, operational, and strategic objectives. Duties typically include such activities as, but not limited to: Manage office operations including file maintenance, database management, organizing departmental meetings, and taking meeting minutes Act as a general resource for researching and preparing cost estimates, completing purchase requisitions, processing invoices and reimbursements, and other similar activities Create, format, and upload examinations in ExamSoft (Web-based assessment software); assist with the proctoring of quizzes, midterm, and final examinations within the BVS and Clinical Education departments; manage student assessments, generate item analyses, post grades, and provide overall examination and assessment support. Assist the Department Chair with budget development, monitoring and analyzing expenditures Support the planning and coordination of departmental meetings, events and projects including handling venue arrangements, catering, RSVPs and logistics Collaborate with the Dean for Academic Affairs to compile data on student performance across the OD Program Maintain faculty records including leave requests and timesheets Support other departments and offices, such as Office of Academic Affairs, as needed Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair or the Dean Respond to inquiries from internal and external stakeholders Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Minimum of three (3) years of experience in a multi-staff administrative office environment. Demonstrated excellence in verbal and written communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office 365 applications, including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Ability to exercise sound independent judgment and maintain strict confidentiality. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Proficiency in Adobe Acrobat and social media platforms Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a college, university, or other higher education environment. Experience supporting high level executives, academic departments, faculty, or student-related programs. Supervisory or lead administrative experience. Demonstrated ability to quickly learn and effectively utilize a variety of software applications, including ExamSoft, SharePoint, Faculty Success, and Brightspace. Strong adaptability and willingness to work in a team environment Salary range is $55,000 to $61,000 and there is also a generous benefit package. 15 days of annual leave and 13 paid holidays per year. We are a qualifying employer in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program. View our Benefits at Glance . About US The State University of New York College of Optometry is dedicated to advancing our mission to serve the public through excellence in education, research, and patient care. We prepare future optometrists, conduct innovative research that enhances quality of life, and deliver exceptional patient care, outreach, and access to eye health services for all who need them. Our community embraces pluralism, respect, critical inquiry, debate, and civil discourse in every aspect of our work. SUNY College of Optometry is an equal opportunity employer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 3472017 Apply by Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
