    "https://sunyopt.peopleadmin.com/postings/2588": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty – Syracuse, NY",
      "description": "SUNY College of Optometry | Clinical Faculty – Syracuse, NY Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Faculty – Syracuse, NY Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Faculty – Syracuse, NY Position Description The State University of New York College of Optometry is accepting applications for full-time clinical faculty for its program located at Upstate Medical University in Syracuse, NY. The inaugural class of students will begin in Fall 2027, offering faculty members the unique opportunity to help shape the development of a new campus while contributing to clinical care, education, and interprofessional collaboration. Successful candidates will be expected to contribute significantly to building the College’s new program in Syracuse while meeting the mission of excellence in patient care, teaching, and scholarly activity. Initial faculty responsibilities will include collaborative planning for program development and didactic teaching in small-group laboratories and seminars. Direct patient care and clinical supervision of students will be incorporated as clinical operations expand. Participation in clinical research is encouraged. Occasional travel to the College’s New York City campus will be expected to support cross-campus collaboration and the integration of the Syracuse campus into the broader College community. SUNY College of Optometry, in partnership with SUNY Upstate Medical University, is dedicated to fostering a vibrant intellectual community of clinicians, educators, and researchers who work together on educational and clinical research initiatives. Candidates should have a record of educational and scholarly activity appropriate for their level of experience. The start date is flexible, with an anticipated appointment beginning in Winter of 2026-27. Clinical faculty at the Syracuse campus will be appointed to the SUNY College of Optometry faculty with all the benefits, responsibilities, expectations, and participation in governance as the faculty at the main campus in New York City. The position requires a Doctor of Optometry degree. Residency training or advanced degrees are highly desirable. Candidates must be licensed or eligible for licensure in New York State at time of hire. The salary range is $102,000 to $130,000. Salary is commensurate with education, training, and experience and includes a generous benefit package with fifteen days of annual leave per year and thirteen paid holidays per year. We are a qualifying employer in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program. View our Benefits at a Glance . Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, a statement of career goals and interests, any representative publications, and the names and contact information of three references. These positions will remain open until filled. About US The State University of New York College of Optometry is dedicated to advancing our mission to serve the public through excellence in education, research, and patient care. We prepare future optometrists, conduct innovative research that enhances quality of life, and deliver exceptional patient care, outreach, and access to eye health services for all who need them. Our community embraces pluralism, respect, critical inquiry, debate, and civil discourse in every aspect of our work. The College’s main campus is in the heart of New York City, adjacent to Bryant Park in Midtown Manhattan, placing students and faculty at the center of one of the world’s most dynamic academic, healthcare, and cultural environments. In addition, the College’s Upstate program offers a unique opportunity to help shape an innovative partnership with SUNY Upstate Medical University, the only teaching hospital in Central New York, advancing interdisciplinary education, patient care, and clinical research. SUNY College of Optometry is an equal opportunity employer. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 3432017 Apply by Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Statement of Career Goals Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Media File Portfolio Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://sunyopt.peopleadmin.com/postings/2585": {
      "title": "Customer Service Representative: Call Center",
      "description": "SUNY College of Optometry | Customer Service Representative: Call Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Customer Service Representative: Call Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Thank you for your interest. We are no longer accepting applications for this position. Please review our current openings to identify opportunities that best match your qualifications and experience. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Customer Service Representative: Call Center Position Description The University Eye Center ( UEC ) is seeking enthusiastic, customer-focused professionals to join our team as Customer Service Representatives in our Call Center. In this role, you will serve as the first point of contact for our patients, creating a welcoming, positive experience and delivering exceptional customer service in a fast-paced healthcare environment. Working collaboratively with providers and staff, you will serve as a liaison between patients, UEC departments, and external healthcare organizations. You will assist patients by scheduling appointments, completing patient registration, verifying insurance eligibility, obtaining authorizations, and responding to patient inquiries. You will also support patient portal enrollment and accurately document patient interactions and demographic information in the NextGen Electronic Health Record ( EHR ) and Practice Management (PM) systems. Additional responsibilities include verifying and communicating patients’ vision and medical insurance benefits and providing information about UEC services and programs. The ideal candidate is organized, detail-oriented, and committed to delivering compassionate, timely, and professional service. This position requires regular on-site attendance at the University Eye Center. Remote work is not available for this role. Required Qualifications Minimum of two (2) years of customer service experience, preferably in healthcare, hospitality, call center, or other client service environments Ability to work evenings and Saturdays Ability to work onsite Excellent organizational skills and strong attention to detail Outstanding verbal and written communication skills Professional telephone etiquette and interpersonal skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, and Excel Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of managed care, insurance verification, authorizations, and third-party payers Experience with Practice Management (PM) and Electronic Health Record ( EHR ) systems, preferably NextGen Bachelor’s degree and/or bilingual proficiency Schedule Tuesday–Thursday: 10:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. Friday: 9:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Saturday: 8:00 a.m. – 4:00 p.m. The salary for this position is $49,373 including location pay. There is also a generous benefits package. 15 days of annual leave per year and 13 paid holidays per year. We are a qualifying employer in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program. View our Benefits at Glance . About US At The University Eye Center ( UEC ), an Article 28 Diagnostic and Treatment Center within the State University of New York, College of Optometry we are inspired to make a difference, and are committed to integrity and excellence. We welcome new ideas and encourage continuous improvement. We strive for a culture that regards people as professionals and will foster trust, commitment, consistency and results. We will strive to have a diverse, collaborative, team-oriented and results-oriented culture. The State University of New York College of Optometry is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or retaliation. To view the College’s Annual Security Report, visit https://sunyopt.edu/?s=annual+security+report Posting Detail Information Posting Number 3462017 Apply by Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Thank you for your interest. We are no longer accepting applications for this position. Please review our current openings to identify opportunities that best match your qualifications and experience. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Can you work the schedule below onsite: Tuesday–Thursday: 10:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. Friday: 9:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Saturday: 8:00 a.m. – 4:00 p.m. Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
