    "https://sunyopt.peopleadmin.com/postings/2579": {
      "title": "Office Assistant 1 (NY HELPS)",
      "description": "SUNY College of Optometry | Office Assistant 1 (NY HELPS) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Office Assistant 1 (NY HELPS) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Thank you for your interest. We are no longer accepting applications for this position. Please review our current openings to identify opportunities that best match your qualifications and experience. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Office Assistant 1 (NY HELPS) Position Description The University Eye Center ( UEC ) of the State University of New York College, is seeking an Office Assistant 1 (NY HELPS ). This title is part of the New York Hiring for emergency Limited Placement Statewide Program (NY HELPS ). Responsibilities/ Job Functions: Greets patients in a professional, courteous manner upon arrival to the service. Interacts with patients to serve their needs and provide assistance and information on the telephone or in person with regard to the services. Prepares all necessary forms that need to be processed for the patient ( HIPAA , assignment of benefits, etc.) and have them scanned into the EMR in a timely manner. Effectively makes the necessary appointments and referrals for services upon exiting. Effectively works with the computer terminals data entry, retrieval, and processing of information in the NextGen and EHR systems, while processing UEC patients. The quality and volume of work must be acceptable and timely. Answers telephones in an appropriate, professional manner and schedules patients in the appropriate slots. Performs the following tasks in the clinic areas: verification of demographic information, print reports and reconcile information, obtain basic insurance information, conduct follow-up on no-show and cancelled appointments, contact the call center to complete insurance during registration, and enter copays/insurance cards. Minimum Requirements Ability to work Evenings and weekends. Ability to work Monday, Thursday and Friday: 8:30-4:30, Tuesday and Wednesday: 12:00-8:00 Ability to provide high-level customer service in a professional, service-oriented, respectful, and friendly manner. Strong attention to detail This position is onsite at 33 West 42nd Street New York, NY 10036 Annual Salary (including location pay) is $40,232 and there is also a generous benefits package. 13 days of annual leave per year and 13 paid holidays per year. We are a qualifying employer in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Program. View our Benefits at a Glance . About US At The University Eye Center ( UEC ), an Article 28 Diagnostic and Treatment Center within the State University of New York, College of Optometry we are inspired to make a difference, and are committed to integrity and excellence. We welcome new ideas and encourage continuous improvement. We strive for a culture that regards people as professionals and will foster trust, commitment, consistency and results. We will strive to have a diverse, collaborative, team-oriented and results-oriented culture. The State University of New York College of Optometry is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or retaliation. To view the College’s Annual Security Report, visit https://sunyopt.edu/?s=annual+security+report Posting Detail Information Posting Number 3452017 Apply by Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Thank you for your interest. We are no longer accepting applications for this position. Please review our current openings to identify opportunities that best match your qualifications and experience. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Can you work the schedule below onsite: Monday, Thursday and Friday: 8:30-4:30, Tuesday and Wednesday: 12:00-8:00 Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Reference Contact Information Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
